Package: ssbmf
Type: Package
Title: Survival-Supervised Bayesian Matrix Factorization
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Andrew", "Walther", email = "awalther@unc.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits a Bayesian matrix factorization of one or more molecular data
    blocks measured on the same patients jointly with a Cox proportional hazards
    model for survival. Patient activities are shared across blocks, feature
    loadings are block specific, and the survival linear predictor is the
    projection of the centered data onto the loadings, so new patients are
    scored in closed form. Priors are fitted by empirical Bayes and the fit
    maximizes one stated variational objective.
